Package: deepblue-security
Version: 1.0.0
Architecture: all
Maintainer: DeepBlue Project <maintainer@deepblue.example>
Installed-Size: 32
Depends: nftables, unattended-upgrades
Recommends: apparmor
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Description: DeepBlue Linux default security hardening
 Turns on the security defaults DeepBlue ships: a default-deny nftables
 firewall, automatic installation of Debian security updates, AppArmor
 enforcement and a hardened kernel sysctl profile. Everything here is plain
 configuration owned by this package, so it can be inspected, changed or
 removed like any other Debian package.
